  "windowPlacementsDescription": "Linear requests whose records, with the IDs `recordIds`, are drawn whole (no `windows`) or in the windows `windows` ([start, end] spans), with Record Order `tokens`, and the cells Python's renderer draws, row by row and left to right (`record-<n>` for a whole record, `record-<n>~w<k>` for its k-th window, `@<row>`); null where it refuses the list. The renderer places a record's windows together, in window order, at its token's place in the row (`_unit_positions`, gbdraw/api/request_render.py); the Web gives each cell its place at Load (`storedLinearCellPlaces`, services/session-request.js). tests/test_web_contracts_generated.py draws each case with `build_request_diagram`; tests/web/stored-request-read.test.mjs loads each into the CLI Session tests/fixtures/sessions/cli-linear-records-table-grid.v51.gbdraw, whose one-record files hold these IDs, and reads the cells of the loaded draft.",
